<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Proclamation of the People's Republic of China</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as founding of the People's Republic of China</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> was proclaimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>, chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a>, on 1 October 1949 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiananmen">Tiananmen</a> Square in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, a ceremony that also proclaimed the Central People's Government and marked the foundation of contemporary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It came as the Communists won the final phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a> against the Kuomintang-led Nationalist government of the Republic of China, which retreated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> by December 1949. At the ceremony the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/march-of-the-volunteers">March of the Volunteers</a> was played as the national anthem, the Five-starred Red Flag was raised for the first time to a 21-gun salute, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-liberation-army">People's Liberation Army</a> held its first public parade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/proclamation-of-the-peoples-republic-of-china.jpg" alt="Proclamation of the People's Republic of China" width="330" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orihara1 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mao_Proclaiming_New_China.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
